---
description: Author Unity objects in the scene or a prefab, not at runtime
alwaysApply: true
---

Screens, canvases, text, images, buttons, lights, cameras, and other editable Unity objects are created as scene objects or prefabs and wired through serialized fields.

Do not build that hierarchy in Awake, Start, or a factory with new GameObject, AddComponent, or RectTransform setup. Runtime code fills in data, shows and hides objects, and spawns instances of an existing prefab.

A large scene file is not a reason to generate the object in code. Create a prefab and place an instance.

Spawn at runtime only for per-play instances of an authored prefab, such as a card or a combat effect.
